NAME
       md5sum - compute and check MD5 checksums

SYNOPSIS
       md5sum [FILE...]
       md5sum -c CHECKSUM-FILE

DESCRIPTION
       md5sum prints the MD5 checksum (32 hexadecimal digits) of each file,
       then its name. With -c it checks the files listed in a checksum file
       and prints OK or FAILED for each. MD5 can be forged on purpose, so use
       it only to spot accidental damage; prefer sha256sum.

OPTIONS
       -c, --check
              Check the files listed in CHECKSUM-FILE.

       --quiet, --status
              With -c, print only failures, or nothing at all.

EXAMPLES
           md5sum /etc/hosts
           md5sum *.iso > sums.md5; md5sum -c sums.md5

SEE ALSO
       sha256sum(1), cksum(1)
